<title>UK: Italy's Oil Energy signs for 10,000 bpd Iraqi crud.</title>
<headline>Italy's Oil Energy signs for 10,000 bpd Iraqi crud.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Italian oil refiner Oil Energy has signed a contract with Iraq to buy 10,000 barrels per day of crude over three months under the U.N. oil-for-food plan, a company spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said Oil Energy's first shipment would load at the Turkish port of Ceyhan in mid-January and sail for Venice, whence it would be pumped into Oil Energy's refinery inland in northeast Italy.</p>
<p>The spokesman said his contract, one of five already approved, was given the green light on Thursday night by the U.N. in New York.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
